<h1 style=3D"margin:0; font-size:30px; line-height:125%"><span style=3D"col=
or: #192733;">Why American cities pay over $3,000 for one trash can</span><=
/h1>
<p style=3D"font-size:18px; line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"font-size:18px; line-height:125%"><span style=3D"color: #192733=
;"><em>High-tech, designer trash bins are popular with local governments. B=
ut many people just want a regular can on the corner.</em></span></p>
<p style=3D"font-size:13px; line-height:125%; font-weight:bold">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"font-size:13px; line-height:125%; font-weight:bold"><br><span s=
tyle=3D"color: #192733;">BY <a href=3D"https://d2q-Vf04.na1.hubspotlinks.co=
m/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VVxthC8x5rDDW5W-rGp2q7Qm5W2bnPc75J_z10N74PqsK2_3wqW5B=
W0B06lZ3m-W4Hv1JD7l_NNgW9kc8VM88QRP4VwX9Vr4jBx3pV60xln6lkFxVW3JKkBr5t5f9xW5=
f-VNR15cT8LW6QZCly5h2LjNN1HrR3PPQ7K6W3_B9Vp5TP7wHW6KfB4k7PnDgzW1-vB-C6TF7Jx=
N2XZXccVpDH1W89x5Pg6qCTLpVRc9gs5BsZhTW5HGCDm3gZKXWW7DXkK23jZDlJW6dZvfs6Znfw=
7W1dWCz_7sqG1Wf8cwjXY04" style=3D"font-weight:bold; color:#192733; text-dec=
oration:none !important" rel=3D"noopener" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-lin=
k-id-v2=3D"dEMdBBbn" target=3D"_blank">MARK DENT</a></span></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%"><em>High-tech, designer trash bins are popula=
r with local governments. But many people just want a regular can on the co=
rner.</em></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">When <strong>Danny Sauter</strong> campaigned=
 door-to-door in northeastern San Francisco in 2024, he expected that resid=
ents would be united over concerns about homelessness and housing costs. Bu=
t a surprising issue kept popping up: trash cans.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Though San Francisco has ~3k of them on its i=
nfamously grimy sidewalks, plenty of residents felt like there weren=E2=80=
=99t enough.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">=E2=80=9CPeople would say, =E2=80=98I can wal=
k 10 blocks without seeing a trash can,=E2=80=99 or =E2=80=98there used to =
be a trash can on this corner for five years, and then it disappeared overn=
ight,=E2=80=99=E2=80=9D says Sauter, who won election as District 3 supervi=
sor.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Early last year, he requested that the city p=
ut <strong>1.5k more cans </strong>in his district. He knows it won=E2=80=
=99t solve everything but believes a strategy of =E2=80=9Cmore trash cans a=
nd more pickups=E2=80=9D would create a cleaner environment.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Public trash cans are a messy problem for Ame=
rican cities. Some municipalities believe that having <em>fewer</em> trash =
cans reduces litter. And some spend upwards of <strong>$3k</strong> for a s=
ingle trash can, believing premium designs and technology will solve their =
problems, only for residents to report similar cleanliness issues as before=
.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">What would seem to be a simple concept =E2=80=
=94 placing enough bins in walkable, trafficked areas and servicing them fr=
equently =E2=80=94 is a fraught endeavor, one that feeds into <a href=3D"ht=
tps://d2q-Vf04.na1.hubspotlinks.com/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VVxthC8x5rDDW5W-rGp=
2q7Qm5W2bnPc75J_z10N74Pqsq4ZD0CW50kH_H6lZ3kCW7xHkcS29SK-vW6mFyg03HycT7W52f2=
1l51wwQMW64_VNq2WT2nQVmWy0l1skSSCW4QXPy73jSDSfW67_RJM6dzX95W6lmKsm3r5JLqV-j=
Pp54c_YfBW4SRx1d5pS0RkW8hZKH_6blPz2W2b8gNd4YKhjtW5KV76Z13WmdwW5gVpRZ2CdcCKW=
5hB9Hy1RhtvWW3rkZHK1bLfm-W7yYlLT58jCPlW65bdvK57vs_MW5kW9kT2HN53HW33VYtl216w=
DJW8Z_cY83B-cYDW6z0JL53RHjjVN8pGbBB9K4yDW1yFsvQ8GHvT3W7ZzQ096pKGJhW4BVbLZ4B=
bX6MW3Csk-k8mbJZXVXTbwd8p6VZ-W1SrbQ_1xJNXHW5w78lF32BdMBN6sPMVhrV87MN3dYLp-3=
nYS0f8PzgDF04" style=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-i=
d-v2=3D"TehDDKCh" target=3D"_blank">the growing belief</a> that the governm=
ent can=E2=80=99t get things done.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Why are public trash cans so complicated and =
expensive?</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<h2 style=3D"margin:0; line-height:125%; font-size:18px">Walt Disney, Tokyo=
, and Gavin Newsom</h2>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Start a conversation with somebody who is int=
erested in trash, and they=E2=80=99re likely to bring up one of two places =
where there practically isn=E2=80=99t any: Disney World or Tokyo.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Legend has it that Walt Disney researched cus=
tomer behavior at amusement parks and concluded that deploying trash cans e=
very 30 feet discouraged littering, leading to an abundance of trash cans o=
n Disney properties. The Magic Kingdom has <a href=3D"https://d2q-Vf04.na1.=
hubspotlinks.com/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VVxthC8x5rDDW5W-rGp2q7Qm5W2bnPc75J_z10=
N74PqtW2_3wqW7Y8-PT6lZ3lPV8cK1b953XshW2qwzSx5B5zYnW1nrr8J7LrxXsW2cGc8H8ShGZ=
