;"><em><span style=3D"font-size: 12px;">Gavin Newsom=E2=80=99s mayoral admi=
nistration led an initiative to reduce the number of San Francisco=E2=80=99=
s trash cans. (Michael Macor/The San Francisco Chronicle via Getty Images)<=
/span></em></span></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Other cities have discovered that removing tr=
ash cans made things worse.</p>
<ul style=3D"line-height:125%">
<li aria-level=3D"1">After the New York City Transit Authority removed bins=
 at a few dozen stations from 2011 to 2014, an audit <a href=3D"https://d2q=
-Vf04.na1.hubspotlinks.com/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VVxthC8x5rDDW5W-rGp2q7Qm5W2b=
nPc75J_z10N74Pqtj2_3wqW6N1vHY6lZ3lxW5Rk5609l13SkW8THXp92KXDZ9W4KcXCc8PHdLmW=
3SgPS84Cf0flW4yNWdl4LCFFVW39JL7H8Gpj15W5Gc08D1b2kmcW1D_SXF4q6tzxW2k4FNB6XTP=
Q4W2gB7S42PGF-pVyGfc17Cn1MrW5Vfr1P44jS8xW39Wk9T7LV-GdVd7_jb4vhdMQW4k0fX13fq=
jPhW4Pfydy75JFz4W1LXtDr1RlktXW3MdBG73DJ36VW610L-P5LYrJSW21J2w428y-jpN32M6wM=
hVcpPW3QkzCs3pNvhrf8kg4mg04" style=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" =
data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"v8O9VU2k" target=3D"_blank">found</a> that at station=
s where receptacles were removed the average amount of bags needed for coll=
ecting litter increased <strong>3.2%</strong> and average track fires incre=
ased <strong>33%</strong>.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>
<li aria-level=3D"1">Philadelphia <a href=3D"https://d2q-Vf04.na1.hubspotli=
nks.com/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VVxthC8x5rDDW5W-rGp2q7Qm5W2bnPc75J_z10N74PqtW2_=
3wqW7Y8-PT6lZ3pHW7VpnY895BzSfW3yf3hh1NTPv6VpCR5Q62C1N_W1ghFZN8QMWkKW2mJbz03=
nSj66W8vPs7L3YqDT7W2qKxzK70LCMvW7q_sZv3t01btW35fQ-r3Pr4ZWW71pLmV5b1kt0W6pnF=
kv2cxxy5W60SSj-8KbdRsW344YY018XX-zW9kfbVs1HtfqVN6w9H-WCgql1W65YnFc2NXnpqW4Q=
F3fF4z2_HTW7YcVXy6HlbqBW4-JC7v1b0lqBW1DhWxB4Gj4gQW2w-Mpt6dvkr9W3cVXp14nhWwj=
W2HbkfK5GB12yN7CwsrXKXSyFN63Yndc8RdyjW4-sFpC8bTHFtf1Xhtcl04" style=3D"color=
:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"Y/BC7N3S" target=3D"_=
blank">tested out</a> various numbers of trash receptacles at select parks =
and commercial corridors, measuring the amount of waste, litter, and staff =
hours needed for pickup. It found that more trash cans correlated with less=
 litter and fewer trash cans correlated with more litter. (<em>The Philadel=
phia Citizen</em> opined on the discovery <a href=3D"https://d2q-Vf04.na1.h=
ubspotlinks.com/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VVxthC8x5rDDW5W-rGp2q7Qm5W2bnPc75J_z10N=
74Pqt02_3wqW69sMD-6lZ3pyW28-1Vz6Blr8LW80010w4JQtDbW1k18xv8QxnbfW2Yb0q36hT6j=
3W164kK136RkBDW5hyQCD6vhxQvW5TwXnM8VvXXdVy__Dt1fgRlHW3VPNWs1Gq4wgW3V2Z721gW=
YbRW3s__572_y9nCW1ZTGdY3zDS4LV8zMlr6Szp9ZW3y518x6Vm5xnN67ZHzlB5fflM34HRhjst=
V_N7ftrxymTwM2W8J11y_77KDFtW82VMKY94Ppx6W6NDzYB8z2l5gf2tD99T04" style=3D"co=
lor:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"DV2n9/dJ" target=
=3D"_blank">with the headline =E2=80=9CWater is Wet.=E2=80=9D</a>)</li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%"><strong>Syon Bhanot</strong>, a Swarthmore Un=
iversity behavioral and public economist who helped with the research in Ph=
iladelphia, says the city ran the experiment because, as in San Francisco, =
significant amounts of litter in Philly come from =E2=80=9Cshort dumping,=
=E2=80=9D when people illegally unload garbage in public areas.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Bhanot says social norms can influence behavi=
or around waste and litter. For instance, if people expect consistent curbs=
ide trash pickup, they might have less incentive to illegally dump a bag ne=
xt to a public trash receptacle in the middle of the week, reducing the nee=
d for receptacles. (Since 2024, Philadelphia <a href=3D"https://d2q-Vf04.na=
1.hubspotlinks.com/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VVxthC8x5rDDW5W-rGp2q7Qm5W2bnPc75J_z=
10N74PqtC2_3wqW7lCdLW6lZ3lxW8NkVbZ8N4l8lW1YhZTB6ZyhjsW1vvpTF3r2pVpW2VZxg92M=
SdY6W2D29wB6XJTN7N8pgDPqM1kyGW7_BC1G8t__lFW7GYpMX4p9QsmW4fqf4K5cTW8lW37wzZz=
539kZrW6zDGrq84b9PYW4q5vZ17RSsfMW7BdF794VL1pjW5C8c6d6WZ5X4W2cTW9r2NqSSSVBKh=
4b3QhpxRW858rXj4_HzCsW2ZCmsb5fyzHYW8Sz7Bf6rgq1WW6bV3J-5gP-zwVGN85D89x9nnW6b=
vWx380W4X7W5g3BBG6GHCBkW5pqvQY97P3Nxf4hR0zx04" style=3D"color:#192733" data=
-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"NhJpBsBu" target=3D"_blank">has emp=
loyed</a> twice-weekly trash pickups in several neighborhoods.)</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">The incentive to litter also comes down to a =
cultural expectation about what others condone, Bhanot says.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">And Tokyo-like expectations don=E2=80=99t exi=
st in most American cities. =E2=80=9CI=E2=80=99d like us to be a bit more o=
f a tidy, polite culture, but we=E2=80=99re not there yet,=E2=80=9D Sauter =
says. That=E2=80=99s why he=E2=80=99d like San Francisco to add more trash =
cans.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">While San Francisco has more bins per capita =
than New York City and less-dense California cities like San Jose, it lags =
behind Washington, DC, which has <strong>~6.6k total trash cans</strong> an=
d is often considered one of America=E2=80=99s cleanest cities.</p></div></=
div></td></tr></tbody></table>
