 the central city. It expects to have ~1.7k bins when the expansion is comp=
lete.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">San Francisco, for now, is keeping its number=
 of trash cans roughly the same while introducing a new model.<br><br></p>
<h2 style=3D"margin:0; line-height:125%; font-size:18px">Paying a trash can=
 premium</h2>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">In December 2022, after years of expensive de=
velopment, testing, public feedback, and the fraud conviction of a former P=
ublic Works director, San Francisco announced it had settled on a trash can=
 of the future to replace its aging fleet: the Slim Silhouette.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%"><br>A stainless steel container with circular=
 openings on its front side for garbage and recycling, it beat out cutting-=
edge <a href=3D"https://d2q-Vf04.na1.hubspotlinks.com/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/V=
VxthC8x5rDDW5W-rGp2q7Qm5W2bnPc75J_z10N74Pqt02_3wqW69sMD-6lZ3nDW3ClpSQ5yX0JG=
