Vdq5KW7NYKXz1-bPjYW7xY2Cf7Y3k9SW6Hslkf6jNZ5XW2VCTVr7gtJCRW7y2Pr67mJgrGW4_xN=
7R1pxj4dW33zjzs3khHHqf1b3Ptb04" style=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D"=
0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"8oV2yf8o" target=3D"_blank">designs such as the Be=
ar Saver and Salt &amp; Pepper</a>. The city paid <span style=3D"font-weigh=
t: bold;">~$19k</span> to build the prototype and reached a deal with a con=
tractor to manufacture the trash cans for <span style=3D"font-weight: bold;=
">~$1.4k each</span>. That doesn=E2=80=99t include installation costs or se=
nsors that will provide an alert when the bins are full.&nbsp; &nbsp;<span =
style=3D"font-size: 12px; color: #000000;"> </span></p></div></div></td></t=
r></tbody></table>
