<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Yet premium models don=E2=80=99t always accom=
plish the goals sought by the cities that buy them.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Several years ago, Tacoma, Washington, tested=
 out smart trash cans made by Bigbelly, a popular brand that offers solar e=
nergy-powered bins with a compacting feature, software connection, and a se=
nsor that goes off when bins are full. Besides the high upfront cost, the c=
ity dealt with software fees and solar panel theft and found the compaction=
 didn=E2=80=99t reduce service costs.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Tacoma has replaced the smart trash cans with=
 non-compacting models by Bigbelly and Storr that cost less than half as mu=
ch.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">=E2=80=9CUltimately, we moved away from solar=
 compaction because the math simply didn't add up for our specific needs,=
=E2=80=9D says city spokesperson <strong>Maria Lee</strong>, over email. =
=E2=80=9CWe found that a simple, fully enclosed can prevents litter just as=
 effectively.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Since Philadelphia went premium in the late 2=
000s and early 2010s, its trash cans have been a point of contention among =
residents and politicians.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%"><br>As part of an effort to reduce trash serv=
ice expenses, the city=E2=80=99s Sanitation Department installed ~1.1k comp=
acting BigBelly trash cans. They cost <span style=3D"font-weight: bold;">~$=
3.7k</span> each and replaced standard <span style=3D"font-weight: bold;">$=
100</span> wire baskets, <a href=3D"https://d2q-Vf04.na1.hubspotlinks.com/C=
tc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VVxthC8x5rDDW5W-rGp2q7Qm5W2bnPc75J_z10N74PqtW2_3wqW7Y8-P=
T6lZ3p9W5l7rKV7fm-35W1cdZnS4RC2lPW8BKg9N1wwgktW2GnHC631B3PFMrTqTKzlbDpW42w8=
RN7n4H4cW7Jm82C213twxW8HCbhW5jYqKYW2DJpXF4R1hP4V7j_4v7Pxj0yW329RHM5wGwM4W4c=
ZmgY5pSr6LW49dzFX8k3QXlW4C-kL46zPS0NW6LBhCY6dt-X4W1yF_6r46shWtN2XGY8Mt4XX5W=
3My9s76kk637W6rpFSt8KB8glW2JgtS375-YZLW68r_bG1Tlwv1W2V9gPJ91d0JTVh5mtK6lLxb=
4W7JWFM_7PHVb2W1vL7d45p6qbhW4Gvqmp8H8rDbf2dgbFx04" style=3D"color:#192733" =
data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"0LDAWiAL" target=3D"_blank">acc=
ording to the Philadelphia City Controller</a>. Because of anticipated lowe=
r service costs, the city expected savings of <span style=3D"font-weight: b=
old;">$13m</span> over 10 years compared to the wire baskets.</p></div></di=
v></td></tr></tbody></table>
