rget=3D"_blank">later wrote</a> that the Sanitation Department didn=E2=80=
=99t integrate the Bigbelly=E2=80=99s sensor system, so the alerts for full=
 bins just went =E2=80=9Cinto the ether.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">A Philadelphia Sanitation Department spokespe=
rson declined an interview but said in an emailed statement that Bigbelly t=
rash cans in the city=E2=80=99s core were emptied once or twice per week, c=
ompared to five times per week for prior trash can models, allowing them to=
 coordinate pickups with regular trash services.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%"><strong>Terrill Haigler</strong>, a former sa=
nitation worker in Philadelphia, often comes across Bigbellies that are ove=
rflowing or damaged. And he says that there aren=E2=80=99t nearly enough, e=
specially in neighborhoods outside the heart of the city.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">=E2=80=9CI believe that Philly is in a trash =
can desert,=E2=80=9D he says.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">So he bought his own inexpensive trash cans.<=
/p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<h2 style=3D"margin:0; line-height:125%; font-size:18px">Wandering the tras=
h can desert</h2>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">While working for the city, Haigler began pos=
ting on social media as <a href=3D"https://d2q-Vf04.na1.hubspotlinks.com/Ct=
c/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VVxthC8x5rDDW5W-rGp2q7Qm5W2bnPc75J_z10N74Pqt02_3wqW69sMD-=
6lZ3ppW7NwqV67cw_MGW1JR53q3VYGS0SJYc3htTxjW2NvWwF1rcG5tW8TPSf43GLJxxW7VQQ_7=
126Dm2W4bP3ns7B7ZpxW3Nsw886_Qzn3W2XKQW67zfRwGW4czyp06KWPVYW6G4BNt3fZb72N7TW=
Cw63282vW6QvbY23r2jfpW8g9ZTh7JVyf2W7WBSJZ4ZS8hqW1CVxwX4cZ1y2W6912tp4z0Y8DW6=
gf05-7vDrh4W6C7xl91cwr25W9cByh28rbvRtf6Xqv2d04" style=3D"color:#192733" dat=
a-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"H/sVHmob" target=3D"_blank">Ya Fav=
 Trashman</a>, sharing details about life as a sanitation worker and advoca=
ting for cleaner streets. He started his own private waste collection busin=
ess in 2021.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">And last year Haigler decided to do something=
 about Philadelphia=E2=80=99s lack of trash cans.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Using grant money, Haigler started a pilot pr=
ogram to put five public trash cans in a North Philadelphia neighborhood. B=
y January, four months into the program, his crew had collected ~4.5 tons o=
f trash. He says neighbors and business owners call if they=E2=80=99re over=
flowing before pickup days and sometimes store the garbage until the crew c=
an get it.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">=E2=80=9CYou start to activate the community,=
=E2=80=9D he says. =E2=80=9CThey=E2=80=99re taking pride.=E2=80=9D</p></div=
></div></td></tr></tbody></table>
